    {
      "paperId": "10.2514/6.2025-0287",
      "doi": "10.2514/6.2025-0287",
      "title": "Test and Evaluation Procedure to Develop a Digital Twin of the Sleeper-Sat",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Reyes Garcia, Mario"
        },
        {
          "name": "Castillo, Jesus"
        },
        {
          "name": "Shirin, Afroza"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "A Digital Twin (DT) is not just a collection of static digital models at the component level of a physical system but a dynamic entity that evolves in parallel with the physical system it mirrors. This evolution starts with physics-based or data-driven physics models representing the physical system and advances to Authoritative Virtualization or DT through continuous data assimilation and ongoing Digital Engineering Test and Evaluation processes. This paper aims to create a mathematical framework for the DE Test and Evaluation Process, which incorporates data assimilation to link physical and digital models, uncertainty quantification, uncertainty propagation, and DT calibration process. This framework will enable the DT to perform operations, control, decision-making, and predictions at scale. The framework will be implemented to develop the DT of the Sleeper-sat to analyze the Sleeper-sat's structural deformation during its deployment in space. The Sleeper-sat will be a variant of previously constructed Sleeper-sats from the Aerospace Center at UTEP. The DT of the Sleeper-sat will be capable of predicting and monitoring structural health during its space operations.",
      "citationCount": 0,
      "openAccess_pdf": {},
