    {
      "paperId": "10.2514/6.2021-0623",
      "doi": "10.2514/6.2021-0623",
      "title": "Programmatic Management for the ABEX CubeSat in a Model Based System Engineering Environment",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Lopez, Victor E."
        },
        {
          "name": "Flint, Alana"
        },
        {
          "name": "Thomas, L. D."
        }
      ],
      "year": 2021,
      "abstract": "View Video Presentation: https://doi.org/10.2514/6.2021-0623.vidThis paper describes how the systems engineering team has applied a Model Based Systems Engineering (MBSE) methodology to the Alabama Burst Energetics eXplorer (ABEX) project, formerly known as the Alabama Experiment for In-situ Shielding (AEGIS). The MBSE approach is based around the development of an Integrated Systems Model (ISM) that contains a model of the system and most of the programmatic information about the project. This paper details how the programmatic aspects of the projects were adapted to be recorded and tracked in the ISM.",
      "citationCount": 0,
